# QA cases

When jagt may open each step of `roles/qa/brief.md.dist` for QA, and what QA may report while the step's turn is open. Copy this
file to `roles/qa/cases.md` to edit a case; a case your copy lacks is read from here. Read only where `roles.qa.enabled` is on.

Each case: `step:` a brief step · `at:` the task's statuses · `by:` jagt, human or master, who sets it off ·
`replies:` what QA may report, its statuses then its kinds (plain, question, wait) · one line saying what the
case is, then the case as WHEN/THEN.

## accept

step: accept
at: DEPLOYED
by: jagt
replies: DEPLOYED, IN_PROGRESS; plain, question, wait
The deploy's pipeline is green and the change read up, so QA checks every criterion of the ticket on the environment.
> WHEN ABC-42 is DEPLOYED, its tracker item open and each target's pipeline green THEN QA opens one check on the tip's sha;
> all rows met → `qa passed`; a row not met → `qa-round`; a row unprovable or no login → a question to you; environment down → wait.

## answered

step: answered
at: DEPLOYED
by: human
replies: DEPLOYED, IN_PROGRESS; plain, question, wait
You answered the question a check stopped on, so QA reads the same sha again with your answer.
> WHEN you answer "login is in the flows repo now" THEN the check runs again on the same sha; a second question is a new turn.

## wait-over

step: wait-over
at: DEPLOYED
by: jagt
replies: DEPLOYED, IN_PROGRESS; plain, question, wait
The environment QA named answers its probe again, so the check runs.
> WHEN the probe QA named at `wait` answers THEN the same check runs; nobody is asked meanwhile.

## decline

step: decline
at: DEPLOYED
by: jagt
replies: DEPLOYED; plain
The session answered a QA round with no change and its reason, so QA reads the reason against its evidence.
> WHEN the session replies `no_changes` with why THEN QA ends the check `declined` with the why on the card, or disputes once.

## again-restarted

step: again
at: DEPLOYED
by: jagt
replies: DEPLOYED, IN_PROGRESS; plain, question, wait
jagt was restarted, so a check whose turn is open and unanswered runs again on the same sha.
> WHEN jagt dies with QA reading ABC-42 THEN the turn and its digest stand, the run repeats, nothing is asked twice.

## again-lifted

step: again
at: DEPLOYED
by: human
replies: DEPLOYED, IN_PROGRESS; plain, question, wait
You lifted the stop on a task whose check never answered, so it runs again on the same sha.
> WHEN a check failed on the spend ceiling and you press `lift` THEN the same check runs once; the failure stays in the record.

## done-by-human

step: done
at: DONE
by: human
replies: DONE; plain
You closed the task, so QA gets the `done` signal with its context and cleans up what the brief says, else nothing.
> WHEN you press `done` on ABC-42 with a check open THEN the turn closes, a late verdict is refused at the door, the brief's cleanup runs.

## done-by-tracker

step: done
at: DONE
by: jagt
replies: DONE; plain
`ticket-close` closed the task, so QA gets the `done` signal with its context and cleans up what the brief says, else nothing.
> WHEN the item reaches `doneStatus` mid-check THEN the same as above; a tracker already closed at DEPLOYED opens no check at all.
